@startuml Sequence_submit_session
' Diagramme de séquence --- Soumission d'une session de formation
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #183D5D
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #183D5D
skinparam ActorFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #2B4B6F
skinparam ArrowColor #2B4B6F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FDF6D8
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9A227

participant "QuizManager\n(Unity)" as Quiz
participant "TynassApiClient\n(Unity)" as Client
participant "Backend REST" as API
database "MongoDB\nAtlas" as DB
actor "Entreprise\n(Dashboard)" as Company

== Fin du quiz ==
Quiz -> Quiz : quiz terminé
Quiz -> API : POST /company/quiz/submit\n{ quizId, answers[] } + device_token
API -> DB : lire les bonnes réponses (correctIndex)
API -> API : calculer le score + passed\n(seuil = passingScore)
API --> Quiz : { score, passed, passingScore }
Quiz -> Quiz : AppSession.QuizScore / QuizPassed

== Soumission de la session ==
Quiz -> Client : construire SessionSubmitPayload
Client -> API : POST /sessions/submit\n{ trainingId, employeeId, score, passed... } + device_token
API -> API : calculer durationSeconds\n(horloge serveur, fiable)
API -> API : incrémenter attemptNumber\n(pre-save hook)
API -> DB : enregistrer la Session
API --> Client : 201 Created
Client --> Quiz : succès -> GoQuizResult()

== Consultation (asynchrone) ==
Company -> API : GET /sessions (dashboard)
API -> DB : lire les sessions de l'entreprise
API --> Company : sessions + scores visibles

note over Client, DB : Le score et "passed" viennent du backend,\njamais calculés côté casque (anti-triche).
@enduml
